A||||6||Greg Piet||EGR Gaskets||||1
Z||000000||Greg Piet||11-06-1999||02:59 PM||||I have a blown EGR gasket, but I am unsure as to what it si officially called.<P>There are 3 gaskets for the EGR on my 85/2.8litre v6<P>one is between the Y pipe and the intermediate section (I need this one)<BR>then one between the EGR valve and the intermediate<BR>then another one from the flex pipe to the intermediate.<P>What the heck are these called, or when one goes to the parts store and orders an EGR gasket you get all three?||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||11-07-1999||12:14 AM||||I made mine out of some dead soft copper. They should never blow out. And they take the heat better||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave85||11-07-1999||08:26 PM||||OK this is too weired!!<BR>I just replaced mine today. I just went down to O'Reilly's and asked for a EGR valve gasket and 10 min. later I was done.  I knew I had an exhaust leak and that turned out to be it.<BR>Please note that you will get a strong burning smell for a few minutes after replacement. <BR>Deffinatly runs better now. TOO quiet now though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||11-08-1999||02:04 AM||||But dave, when you go thte egr gasket for 10 bucks, did it have all 3 gaskets?<BR>on checkers magical computer it said EGR gasket (singular) and they had to order it so I was waondering if when you get an EGR gasket does i come with all 3?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave85||11-08-1999||07:49 AM||||If you ask for the EGR gasket you should get 1, The one that goes under the valve. The cost was $1.50 tax included.  I don't know about the others.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||11-10-1999||08:28 AM||||Here are the EGR gasket part numbers from the 22-P manual<P>Gasket, EGR VLV ADAPT TO EXH CR/OVR 10038299<BR>(this is the gasket between the EGR valve and the cross over pipe flange)<P>GASKET, EGR VLV TO ADAP   10038298<BR>(this is the gasket between the two body parts of the EGR valve)<P>GASKET, EGR VLV TRFR TUBE (66MM LG) 10038300<BR>(there are two of these, one at each end of the EGR tube)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Greg Piet||11-10-1999||10:55 PM||||Thanks for the part numbers!<BR>I got the two gaskets(10038298 and 10038300), which Pep Boys had to special order.  They gave me 10 of each, but still not the lower gasket(10038299).  Grrrr  thats the one I need!<BR>I guess ill have to make one myself with copper!||||reg||1
